[[Category:Mining Tools]]

{{GM|$Craft|$Clothes & Equipment|$Tools|$Axes|$Pick Axe}}

==How to Acquire==

[[File:Pickaxe in-game.png|frame|In-game example of a pickaxe]]

You need to equip a [[Smithy's Hammer]] and you need an [[Anvil]] to make a pickaxe.

==Quality==

* [[{{PAGENAME}}]] Quality = <math>\frac{\frac{_{q}Metal+ _{q}Bough}{2} *  9 + {_{q}Anvil* 4 + _{q}Smithy's Hammer}* 3}{16}</math> and is [[softcap|softcapped]] by <math>\sqrt[3]{Strength *Smithing*Masonry}</math>.

==Notes==

* Increases [[Mining]] speed.
* Increases [[Stone|Chip Stone]] Speed.
* Drains the same amount of stamina per tick as an axe. This means that your stamina will drain quicker, as it mines much faster. 
* Allows boulders to be removed from a [[Cellar]] so it can be used. 
* Increases damage of destruction +2 damage to buildings. 
* 2 hand tool. 
* Your mining power with the pickaxe is <math>\sqrt[2]{({q}Pickaxe*2) *Strength}</math> . This means having a better quality pickaxe weighs more than having high strength.
*Counts as a heavy, edged weapon
*
Example: q40 pickaxe and 100 strength is much better than q10 pickaxe and 300+ strength.

